12.

MATTERS TO BE STATED IN A HEALTH INSURANCE POLICY : 
1.

A health insurance policy shall clearly state: 
(i) The name of the policyholder and the names of each beneficiary covered , UIN of the product, 
name, code number, contact details of the person involved in sales process; 
(ii) Date of birth of the insured and corresponding age in completed years; 
(iii) The address of the insured; 
(iv) The period of insurance and the date from which the policyholder has been continuously 
obtaining health insurance cover in India from any of the insurers without break; 
(v) The sums Insured; 
(vi) The sub-limits, Proportionate Deductions and the existence of Package rates if any, with cross-reference to the concerned policy section; 
(vii) Co-pay limits if any; 
(viii) The pre-existing disease (PED) waiting period, if applicable; 
(ix) Specific waiting periods as applicable; 
(x) Deductible as applicable – general and specific, if any;

